  "live_records": {
    "q-34503": {
      "dom_id": "step-q34503",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The matrix $K$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(K).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{k}_{1}+{x}_{2}{k}_{2},$ and ${k}_{1},$ ${k}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $K.$\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(K),$ we need to check if the equation $Kx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[K\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 0=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=-18.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(K).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
