    "q-74213": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74213",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix given by $M=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2k+10\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(M).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ then the equation $Mx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 15 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2k-10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=2k-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=2k-10,$ which means that $k=5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
