    "q-110975": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110975",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ k+5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -2 & k+5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k+40\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+30\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 0=k+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+30,$ which means that $k=-30.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
