    "q-111046": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111046",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The matrix $D$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(D).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}+{x}_{3}{d}_{3}+{x}_{4}{d}_{4},$ and ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, ${d}_{3}$, and ${d}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $Dx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4}=1 \\\\ 0=6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the  second equation, we get a false statement $0=6.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
